==In animation==
===''Pokémon the Series''===
===={{aniseries|BW}}====
[[File:BW024-unaired.png|thumb|left|250px|Team Plasma Grunts in the unaired episodes]]
[[File:Team Plasma anime.png|thumb|250px|Team Plasma Grunts (Aldith in the center) in {{aniseries|BW}}]]
Several Plasma Grunts made an appearance in ''[[BW112|Team Plasma's Pokémon Power Plot!]]'', debuting in their new outfits. They were protecting [[Colress]] while he was conducting his research of how to control [[wild Pokémon]] with special sonic devices. After {{TRT}} had arrived and stolen his research data, Colress and the grunts left the location, destroying the place with a self-destruct mechanism as they did. They also served a payback for Team Rocket for their deeds by blowing up their [[Team Rocket's mechas|balloon]] with a missile fired from their aircraft, sending the trio blasting off again.

They were originally supposed to appear in their older uniforms in [[BW023 (unaired)]] and [[BW024 (unaired)]] in a confrontation with [[Team Rocket]], but the episode was postponed due to the {{wp|2011 Tōhoku earthquake and tsunami|Tōhoku earthquake and tsunami}} and the {{wp|Fukushima Daiichi nuclear disaster}} and, as of ''[[BW112|Team Plasma's Pokémon Power Plot!]]'', retconned from continuity.

Unlike previous [[villainous team]]s in the {{pkmn|animated series}}, some Plasma Grunts have been referred to by name. [[Aldith]], a grunt based on the female Plasma Grunt design from [[Pokémon Black and White Versions 2|Pokémon Black 2 and White 2]], has been assisting Colress and seems to have a slightly higher position amongst the grunts. Two male grunts, [[Schwarz and Weiss]], served as antagonistic [[Character of the day|characters of the day]], attacking N when he tried to free an injured {{p|Braviary}}. In ''[[BW118|Secrets From Out of the Fog!]]'', [[Barret]] appeared, a grunt based on the male Plasma Grunt design from Pokémon Black 2 and White 2. He, with two other grunts, attacked the house where N, [[Anthea and Concordia|Anthea, and Concordia]] were hiding. Like Aldith, he seems to have a slightly higher position than the other grunts.

Multiple Team Plasma Grunts appeared in ''[[M16|Genesect and the Legend Awakened]]'', in a flashback explaining the origins of the [[Genesect Army]].

