==In the manga==
===Pokémon Adventures===
[[File:Team Plasma Grunt Adventures.png|thumb|left|230px|Team Plasma Grunts in the {{MangaArc|Black & White}}]]
[[File:Team Plasma Grunt B2W2 Adventures.png|thumb|200px|Team Plasma Grunts in the {{MangaArc|Black 2 & White 2}}]]
===={{MangaArc|Black & White}}====
Team Plasma Grunts debuted in this chapter. Each of the [[Seven Sages]] has several Grunts working as their subordinates. The only exception is [[Ghetsis]], who has the [[Shadow Triad]] as his subordinates.

Team Plasma Grunts debuted in ''[[PS466|An Odd Speech]]'', where two prepared a stage for Team Plasma to use with a group of {{p|Timburr}}. The act of creating the stage disturbed {{adv|Black}} and {{adv|White}}, who had been camping there for the night. After Black had stopped the Timburr, the Grunts revealed themselves and apologized for the inconvenience. After showing they have the proper permit to build the stage, Black and White apologized for the trouble and moved their camp to sleep elsewhere.

Multiple Team Plasma Grunts, including Gorm's subordinates appeared in ''[[PS496|Museum Showdown]]''. They were tasked with finding the [[Dark Stone]] at the Nacrene Museum. They were stopped by Black, who attacked the Grunts while the Unova Gym Leaders were busy with the Shadow Triad. In ''[[PS497|Finding Truth]]'', one Grunt disguised himself as [[Brycen]] to trick Black into revealing the location where the Dark Stone was kept. After opening the lock to the Dark Stone's safe, Ghetsis revealed himself and knocked Black unconscious. The Grunt then took the Dark Stone and presented it to Ghetsis, who later gave it to N.

When Team Plasma attacked the {{un|Pokémon League}} in ''[[PS520|Cold Hard Truth]]'', several Team Plasma Grunts emerged from [[N's Castle]] and surrounded everyone inside the area. The Grunts, including [[Giallo]]'s subordinates, proclaimed that the day would mark a new day for Team Plasma, as they are aided by N, the King of Team Plasma, who is aided by the power of {{DL|Tao trio (Adventures)|Zekrom}}. After the captured Gym Leaders were freed from Team Plasma's grasp, they and several other Trainers battled the Grunts to save the League spectators.

===={{MangaArc|Black 2 & White 2}}====
After Team Plasma's defeat, several Team Plasma Grunts, including {{adv|Whitley}} and her {{OBP|Mom|Black 2 and White 2|mother}}, escaped from N's Castle to avoid being arrested. Whitley would later become a [[Pokédex holder]] in this chapter.

In ''[[PS531|Unforgettable Memories]]'', two Team Plasma Grunts show [[Colress]] the new Team Plasma Grunt uniform.

In ''[[PS533|New Sword Player]]'', Giallo was attacked by {{DL|Forces of nature (Adventures)|Tornadus}}. After {{adv|Blake}} managed to {{status|freeze}} Tornadus, the Grunts controlling it recalled it and escaped. 

In ''[[PS535|Angry Boy]]'', Blake, Whitley, [[Hugh]], and [[Roxie]] entered the [[Castelia Sewers]] after finding a man whose Pokémon was liberated by Team Plasma. After exploring the area, they found a room of Team Plasma Grunts, along with Bronius and Ryoku. Out of anger from his sister's Purrloin being stolen, Hugh rashly attacked the Grunts, leaving him open to be swarmed by the Grunts' Pokémon forcing to the group to scatter. Later, Whitley and Roxie were cornered by the Grunts, forcing Roxie to fight them off. Whitley managed to easily defeat the Grunts' Pokémon forcing them to release their liberated Pokémon and escape.

In ''[[PS543|Abyssal Ruins]]'', four Grunts attacked [[Rood]] and Hugh in order to prevent them from obtaining a memory card containing data on a machine that would counteract that [[Colress Machine]]. Hugh chose to stay behind to fight the Grunts while Rood went on ahead to get the memory card.

