====Subordinates====
=====Gorm's subordinates=====
[[File:Gorm subordinates Adventures.png|thumb|200px|Gorm's subordinates in Pokémon Adventures]]
In ''[[PS471|Battle at the Dreamyard]]'', [[Gorm]]'s subordinates captured Black's [[Musha]] after it was lured to the [[Dreamyard]] by the lingering dreams of the people who once worked there. The three Grunts battled Black in order to liberate Musha back into the wild, but Musha's love of Black's dreams caused it to run back to its Trainer. After being defeated, the Grunts ran away, leaving behind the {{p|Watchog}} they used to battle Black.

In ''[[PS475|The Mystery of the Missing Fossil]]'', Gorm and his subordinates steal the [[Dragon Skull|Dragon Fossil]] from the {{DL|Nacrene City|Nacrene Museum}}. Using Gorm's {{p|Cofagrigus}} to manipulate the skeleton, they were able to make it walk around as if it was alive. Black managed to track the thieves down with the help of Musha. They were defeated when Black and [[Burgh]] defeated Cofagrigus, preventing Gorm and the Grunts from controlling the skeleton. Afterward, Gorm and the Grunts escaped

Gorm's subordinates appeared in ''[[PS496|Museum Showdown]]'', where they were tasked with finding the [[Dark Stone]] at the Nacrene Museum. They were stopped by Black, who attacked the Grunts while the Unova Gym Leaders were busy with the Shadow Triad. After the Gym Leaders were captured by Team Plasma, Gorm's subordinates and the other Grunts retreated.

In ''[[PS539|Frozen World]]'', it was revealed that one of Gorm's subordinates used to work at a [[Pokémon Center]].

